    "Notes Updated": "9/18/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "First full pro season in the rear view\n Dealt with a lot of injuries, but performed pretty decently when out there\n Tools are evident, speed is plus plus if not elite\n There's legit power in there, and he seemed to aim to tap into it a bit more\n Stance/swing change in July is something I really like, there are some Yelich similarities now, though he will need to smoothen it out a bit\n Speed is great, but like many young players, learning to be a baserunner and not just a speed demon will be important\n Defense is a WIP, but he has all the tools to play a good centerfield and the arm looks average or a bit better.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "9/15/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Raw power is already showing in his early pro ball debut\n Up to 110 MPH EV's and reportedly even 111 in instructs\n Speed is very noticeable as a base stealer and in general, and he plays super hard\n Think there is some swing and miss on high fastballs, but mostly due to an aggressive approach on them.\n General plate discipline is quite solid.\n Defense is a WIP, but he has all the tools to play a good centerfield",
    "Notes Updated 3": "7/20/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 3": "Post Draft 2024\n  Very fast, very athletic in general\n  Bat to ball skills are strong, swing has improved over time to help get a little more lift on the ball\n  Rising player who has made huge strides\n  Very young, not quite 18 yet\n  Scouts think there is raw power in there\n  Kind of reminds me of a combo of Garrett Mitchell and Brice Turang",
    "Notes Updated 4": "N/A",
